    "tallis": {
      "headline": "A below-cost investment needs better engagement economics and cash delivery",
      "word_count": 179,
      "sections": [
        {
          "heading": "Business Overview",
          "basis": "Illustrative business context",
          "text": "Tallis provides tax, accounting, audit and advisory services. In this illustrative business model, business owners, trusts and individual clients buy professional time, recurring compliance work and selected advisory projects; returns depend on billable utilization, realization and durable partner-led client relationships."
        },
        {
          "heading": "What's Working",
          "basis": "Reported indicators \u00b7 Illustrative investment context",
          "text": "Legacy September revenue growth is a favorable single-month indicator. The range of services creates a potential opportunity to deepen client relationships, but cross-selling and sustained organic growth have not been demonstrated. Those opportunities matter because the illustrative investment remains below cost, with a negative gross IRR."
        },
        {
          "heading": "What's Under Pressure",
          "basis": "Source-backed operating review",
          "text": "The September monthly review and YTD earnings comparison both miss plan. Partner-compensation pressure, Redfern\u2019s weak realization and aged work-in-progress, and Ashcombe\u2019s retention gap put recovery at risk. Acquisition effects cloud growth comparisons, while prospective compensation savings do not establish realized earnings or a dependable recovery run rate."
        },
        {
          "heading": "Operational Priorities",
          "basis": "Proposed initiatives \u00b7 Not established causes",
          "text": "Review engagement staffing and billing: compare billable utilization with realization, clear aged work-in-progress and assign collection owners. Test fixed-fee job economics before repricing, align partner compensation with evidenced performance, and review at-risk client relationships. Treat cross-selling and prospective savings as initiatives to validate, not committed earnings."
        }
      ],
