    "harrow": {
      "headline": "Positive illustrative returns need reliable fleet capacity and cash conversion",
      "word_count": 176,
      "sections": [
        {
          "heading": "Business Overview",
          "basis": "Illustrative business context",
          "text": "Harrow\u2019s reported activities include commercial collection, roll-off and industrial work, recycling and processing. The illustrative business model serves commercial and industrial customers through trucks, routes and customer contracts; economics depend on route density, fleet utilization, disposal costs and disciplined asset replacement."
        },
        {
          "heading": "What's Working",
          "basis": "Reported indicators \u00b7 Illustrative investment context",
          "text": "North\u2019s higher tons per route-day is an observed physical productivity improvement, and the illustrative ledger shows positive investment returns. Listed contract wins offer potential growth, but their commencement, retention and cash contribution remain unverified. Route-density gains or benefits from routing software have not been established."
        },
        {
          "heading": "What's Under Pressure",
          "basis": "Source-backed operating review",
          "text": "FY2026 annual EBITDA missed budget despite revenue growth. South\u2019s downtime and rental needs, weaker cash conversion after obligations and capital requirements temper the investment case. Major-account contract renewals and East\u2019s disposal-cost pressure require attention. Rental and commodity adjustments should not substitute for demonstrated operating improvement."
        },
        {
          "heading": "Operational Priorities",
          "basis": "Proposed initiatives \u00b7 Not established causes",
          "text": "Prioritize maintenance triage and measure completed repairs against availability, rentals and truck utilization. Test route density and service profitability before adding capacity; sequence capital spending against cash available after debt obligations. Prepare account-specific renewal plans and validate new-contract start dates, service costs and realized contribution."
        }
      ],
